  "analysis": [
    {
      "label": "Context",
      "text": "Chelsea had raced into a 3–0 lead early on and led 3–1 on the night, 4–3 on aggregate. Barcelona needed one more goal, which would have put them through on away goals."
    },
    {
      "label": "Build-up",
      "text": "Iniesta carried the ball up through midfield and fed Ronaldinho on the edge of the box. With Carvalho set in front, there was no run in behind to aim for, so the space had to be made from a standing start."
    },
    {
      "label": "Key moment",
      "text": "Carvalho held a tight, square stance in front of Ronaldinho. A sway of the hips, with the ball barely moving, got the defender to shift weight the wrong way, which opened just enough of a shooting lane."
    },
    {
      "label": "The finish",
      "text": "The toe-poke needed no backlift, so there was no cue to read. Čech was set for a wind-up that never came and hardly moved as the ball went low towards the corner."
    }
  ]
